Z||000000||JohnnyK||10-06-2000||03:50 PM||||I don't think this is normal, and part of my problem... I have it all apart, and where the release bearing rubs against the middle of the pressure plate (right on the edge of the springs) it is shiny and worn down maybe 1/16 or 1/8. I assume this is because it is staying there. Could this be the problem that I read about (Clutch fork bushings too tight?) Thanks! ||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||10-06-2000||05:01 PM||||thats how the clutch works.. and with high mileage and ridding the clutch that where its gunna wear.. along with the disc surface... but if the bearing siezed up it will trash that area more but SQUEEL REALLY LOUD!||||reg||1
