Z||000003||StuGood||10-06-2000||06:05 PM||||Seems like a good idea to replace disc, pressure plate and T/O bearing as long as you've got it all apart.  ||||reg||3
Z||000004||Phil||10-06-2000||06:26 PM||||Read an article(forgot where)that said that the TO bearing should have about .006" clearance on the input shaft. Their quick of checking was to wrap a piece of paper around the shaft and the TO bearing should slide over it. Same deal on the fork shaft. FWIW||||reg||1
